# DRAFT environment mapping for `poudriere bulk` under a retained run.
#
# Sourced by run-bulk.sh with `set -a`; the retained profile cannot pass environment variables.
# Grounded:  the registered release jail name (`16r2303b36`) and the shape of the poudriere
#            etc/data split follow the daemonarchy product repo's scripts/master-release.sh and
#            docs/mastering-1.5.0.md (always `poudriere -e $WORK/poudriere-etc`); the jail and
#            registry files exist on mudflap (poudriere-etc/poudriere.d/jails/16r2303b36).
# UNKNOWN:   whether this release jail, rather than the HACKING.md example `16amd64`, is the right
#            one for ports-tree validation; HACKING.md names `16amd64`/`omarchyiso`, which are not
#            registered on mudflap. The ports tree here is the retained snapshot itself, registered
#            at run time under the name PTREE (null method, no copy).
WORK=/usr/daemonarchy/rev2-20261030
POUDRIERE_ETC_SOURCE=$WORK/poudriere-etc
JAIL=16r2303b36
PTREE=retained
ORIGINS=Tools/daemonarchy/retained/origins.draft.list
